  <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container split"><div><span class="kicker">How VPN4U works</span><h2>Independent service, established infrastructure.</h2><p>We source capacity from established datacentre and network operators, then provide the customer-facing service under VPN4U. Customers deal with VPN4U for the order, service description, provisioning communication and support.</p><p>We do not claim to own every underlying datacentre, server or network. Our role is to package suitable infrastructure into clearly described services and remain accountable for the commercial relationship.</p><a class="textLink" href="/infrastructure">Read about our infrastructure model →</a></div><div class="principles"><div><strong>01</strong><span><b>Clear specifications</b><small>CPU, memory, storage, traffic, location and delivery model are described before the order is accepted.</small></span></div><div><strong>02</strong><span><b>Availability confirmed first</b><small>Dedicated stock and regional availability are checked before payment is requested.</small></span></div><div><strong>03</strong><span><b>One point of contact</b><small>VPN4U remains the commercial and support contact for the service you purchase.</small></span></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="sectionHead"><div><span class="kicker">Built around real service delivery</span><h2>What customers can expect</h2></div><p>We keep the ordering model deliberately simple and avoid promises that do not apply equally to every infrastructure location.</p></div><div class="featureGrid">
    <article><h3>Order review first</h3><p>Submitting an order request does not charge you. We verify availability and material configuration details before payment is requested.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Transparent service scope</h3><p>Standard VPS and dedicated products are infrastructure services. Managed administration is included only when explicitly stated.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Published policies</h3><p>Terms, privacy, acceptable use, cancellations, refunds, cookies and abuse-reporting information are available from every page.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Dedicated support channels</h3><p>Separate sales, support, abuse and privacy email addresses make it clear where each type of request should go.</p></article>
  </div></div></section>

  <section class="section sectionMuted"><div class="container proseGrid"><div><span class="kicker">For individuals & developers</span><h2>Start small and keep control.</h2><p>Run websites, APIs, development environments, self-hosted services or private connectivity without buying into a large enterprise platform. Standard products are designed to be understandable from the specification alone.</p><a class="textLink" href="/faq">Read common questions →</a></div><div><span class="kicker">For businesses</span><h2>Ask for a configuration review.</h2><p>If you need a particular location, larger memory footprint, dedicated hardware, software licence or network requirement, send the specification to sales. We can confirm whether a standard or custom option is appropriate.</p><a class="textLink" href="/contact">Talk to sales →</a></div></div></section>

